 ### Stage S3 — working space
+**Status: implemented 2026-08-28** (`scene` commits: matrices + main-target fp16 floor, the
+conversion node, the luminance weights, the boundary audit). The conversion is an in-place compute
+dispatch on `$HDRTarget`'s UAV between the `$HDRTargetPrev` copy and the depth-of-field stage;
+`$HDRTargetPrev` deliberately stays Rec.709 for SSR, the water reflection and the SVOGI bounce, and
+motion blur's history selector was fixed to match. `r_SceneReferredDebug` is the stage's A/B and
+its acceptance instrument. Two amendments earned here: the AP1 luminance weights arrive as a
+per-view **constant** (stored as a delta from Rec.709) rather than as the shader permutation §5
+implied, because the DOF gather evaluates them 121 times per pixel; and the third bullet's clamp
+sweep came back **empty** — every colour-data clamp between the HDR target and the tone map is
+already owned by S0 (formats), S2 (the shafts), S4 (the display wall) or S7 (thresholds), and our
+own effects clamp nothing but masks. Recorded in `scene-notes/research/s3-luminance-and-saturates.md`
+§9 and `scene-notes/STRUCTURE.md` §7b. **Until S4 lands the picture will look slightly wrong** —
+the Hable curve and the sRGB encode are being fed AP1 values as if they were Rec.709.
